			"notes": "Adds Experiment 8, a new worked-example bench demonstrating the Bundler/Unbundler pair in both directions:\n\n**3-Phase Source → Unbundler → three separate mono Resistors (one per split-out phase) → Bundler → 3-Phase Resistor → Ground**, with the final bundle run closing directly at Ground — no second Unbundler needed, since Ground has been bundle-conductive since v0.9.1.\n\n```\n/function circuitsimcraft:three_phase_bundle_unbundle\n```\n\nVerified end-to-end via a real headless test: every mono resistor reads exactly half its phase's source voltage (Ohm's law exact at 100Ω), and the reunited 3-Phase Resistor's three channels still sum to exactly zero, confirming the balanced-three-phase signature survives the full round trip.\n\nsha256: `9a0a900d89dcb55d900bf54e78c31bf66515460348ed4538edd2de19b19675f6`"
		},
