			"notes": "Patch release fixing two build-quality issues in all three villager workshop functions.\n\n- **Floor gap outside every workshop.** The footing beneath each workshop's floor spanned a wider area than the floor layer itself, leaving an unfilled gap at walking level right around the building — most noticeable stepping out the door onto nothing. Floor now matches the footing's full extent in all three (`electrician_shop`, `engineer_workshop`, `electrical_engineer_workshop`).\n- **Iron doors that couldn't be opened.** The Electronics Engineer's and Electrical Engineer's workshops both used an iron door, which needs a redstone signal to open — neither building provides one. Switched to spruce and dark oak respectively, matching each building's palette (the Electrician's shop already used oak).\n- Also fixed a stale \"Known limitations (v0.8)\" heading in the README, three releases out of date, and noted that AC/Bode-plot analysis doesn't cover the Three-Phase Components yet either.\n\nsha256: `5a9cb5add271de92fd66831c20670588c844dda74c2069da649f721a89c3b706`"
		}
